sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Operative as Admin / Student Operative
    participant UI as React File Upload Component
    participant Client as Browser File API & FileReader
    participant API as Express Server (/api/storage & /api/admin)
    participant GridFS as MongoDB GridFS Bucket (attachments)
    participant DB as MongoDB Atlas Collections

    Note over Operative, DB: 1. INLINE PREVIEW & CLIENT-SIDE VALIDATION
    Operative->>UI: Select File (Image / PDF / Document)
    UI->>Client: Validate file.type (image/png, image/jpeg, application/pdf)
    UI->>Client: Validate file.size (Cover: 5MB, QR: 2MB, PDF Spec: 15MB)
    alt Validation Fails
        UI-->>Operative: Toast Error ("File exceeds limit" / "Invalid format")
    else Validation Passes
        Client->>Client: FileReader.readAsDataURL(file)
        Client-->>UI: Display instant preview thumbnail & removal control
    end

    Note over Operative, DB: 2. PERSISTENCE WORKFLOW (GridFS & Base64 Metadata)
    Operative->>UI: Submit Event / Certificate / Payment Proof
    UI->>API: POST /api/admin/certificates/upload OR /api/hackathons (with fileData)
    API->>API: Server-side MIME validation & payload size audit
    alt Large Media (> 500KB)
        API->>GridFS: Open upload stream into fs.files & fs.chunks
        GridFS-->>API: Return GridFS fileId (ObjectId)
        API->>DB: Persist document with { fileId, originalName, mimeType, size }
    else Lightweight Media / Data URLs (QR / Avatars)
        API->>DB: Persist clean data URL / sanitized URI in entity schema
    end
    API-->>UI: 200 OK / 201 Created { success: true, assetUrl }
    UI-->>Operative: Render success feedback & update asset status

    Note over Operative, DB: 3. RETRIEVAL & ACCESS CONTROL
    Operative->>UI: Request asset (e.g. /api/certificates/:id/download)
    UI->>API: GET /api/certificates/:id (Authorization: Bearer <JWT>)
    API->>API: Validate user ownership or administrative clearance
    alt Unauthorized
        API-->>UI: 403 Forbidden ("Unauthorized asset access")
    else Authorized
        API->>GridFS: Stream file chunks from MongoDB Atlas
        GridFS-->>API: Binary file stream
        API-->>Operative: HTTP 200 with Content-Disposition & Content-Type
    end
